routing.lifecycle-campaign-tagging-steward:
# AGENTS

When the traffic sources are clean and the funnel can be split properly:
  @Storefront Funnel Analyst, please rebuild the funnel on the corrected source values.

When a recovery message is being built and the links need tagging:
  @Lifecycle Flow Auditor, please use the published vocabulary rather than hand-writing the parameters.

routing.lifecycle-checkout-auditor:
# AGENTS

When the recovery belongs in a message rather than on the page:
  @Lifecycle Flow Auditor, please specify the recovery sequence for this abandonment point.

When a fix has shipped and the effect needs measuring honestly:
  @Storefront Funnel Analyst, please re-measure the step and tell me whether the change is inside the noise.

routing.lifecycle-flow-auditor:
# AGENTS

When the recovery message lands on a page that undoes it:
  @Checkout Experience Auditor, please audit the landing step for the friction the message cannot fix.

When the flow revenue claim depends on an attribution window nobody agreed:
  @Campaign Tagging Steward, please settle the window before I report the number.

routing.lifecycle-storefront-funnel-analyst:
# AGENTS

When the losing step is known and the screen needs diagnosing:
  @Checkout Experience Auditor, please walk this step on a phone and return a ranked friction list.

When a source split makes the funnel unreadable:
  @Campaign Tagging Steward, please merge the duplicate sources so I can split the funnel properly.

When the loss is after the visit rather than during it:
  @Lifecycle Flow Auditor, please check whether a recovery flow exists for this moment.
